run Bazel build over resolved targets

Usage: dx build [--here] [--affected [--since <ref>]] [--debug|--release] [--timings] [--no-retry] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

  -q, --quiet
          Hide summaries

  -v, --verbose
          Show more logs

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --build-slots <auto|n|off>
          Set build slots: auto, a count, or off

      --build-slots-wait <duration>
          Give up waiting for a build slot after this long; 0 fails at once

      --bazel-startup-option <TOKEN>
          Pass one Bazel startup option (repeatable)

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format
          
          [possible values: text, json]

      --debug
          Use debug build

      --release
          Use release build (the deploy default)

      --timings
          Print where build time went

      --no-retry
          Do not rerun without the remote cache after a remote cache error

      --report <REPORT>
          Write a report file

      --here
          Use the current dir tree

      --affected
          Select targets affected by git changes

      --since <REF>
          With --affected, compare against this ref instead of the default branch merge-base

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  dx build //...
  dx build --release //app -- --local_resources=cpu=4
Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. With no scope, this command runs //...; pass --affected to run only what your changes reach. Pass --here for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes. --affected selects targets changed since the default branch merge-base (or the ref given with --since) plus their reverse dependencies; it cannot be combined with scopes or --here.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|json (json streams events while the command runs); --report failures=<destination> (repeatable).
Environment: NO_COLOR=<non-empty> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

